{
  "dom_id": "question-343869",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14194326/assets/fd917228308b839be77110b07e32fa0154350c290920628400bd1f20a34160b5.png)\n\nA factory tracks the number of defective items remaining after a recall. The number of defective items after $x$ days, in hundreds, is given by the function $N(x).$ The graph of $N(x)$ is shown above.  \n\nApproximate the rate of change when $x=15$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=5.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=10$ and $x=15.$*\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $x=15$ is\n{{field-1}} hundred items per day.",
